※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4615

※ `λ … [n] in pool` keeps what the lambda brought in in the arena, so the lambda is
※ made in it as a string written `in pool` is -- and once the arena is given
※ back, calling the lambda would read what went with it.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 1u8
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let k: fn(u8) → u8 = λ x: u8 [n] in pool → u8 { x + n }
    ⎕empty(pool)
    if k(1u8) = 2u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
